#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess: a two-player (hot-seat) Quick Game played to checkmate, with its capture cartoon
# (#158). Extends throne-room.route from the Quick Game screen: toggles Black from computer to
# human (keeping both sides on the matched Western set with capture animations on), starts the
# game, plays Scholar's Mate (1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nc6 3. Qh5 Nf6 4. Qxf7#), watches the Western
# Queen-captures-Pawn 3D capture cartoon through to "Checkmate! Congratulations, you win!", clicks
# the green tick back to the throne room, and closes the window cleanly.
#
# Replay it with a fresh `--data-root <empty dir>`, never beside the rip, for the same reason as
# throne-room.route: it reaches the New Player form only with no profile saved, and writes
# profiles\prof1.lcp and profiles\1save.lcs.
#
# From flip 432 on the Quick Game screen:
# - (520,180) toggles Black's player button from computer to human (flip 440, let go at poll 300).
# - (590,410) clicks the green tick to start the Western match (flip 450, let go at poll 300).
#   The engine allocates its working table with GlobalAlloc/GlobalLock, the board decodes its two
#   Western board sounds and opens both 16-bit Video 1 Advisors (sherriff.avi, baddude.avi), and
#   wtune.mid plays on the GS Wavetable synth.
# - In two-player mode the board rotates 180 degrees after each move so the side to move is at
#   the bottom. Each ply clicks the source square (held 3 flips) and then the destination square:
#     1. e2-e4   (White, normal view)       flip 560..581
#     1... e7-e5 (Black, rotated view)      flip 730..751
#     2. Bf1-c4  (White, normal view)       flip 900..921
#     2... Nb8-c6 (Black, rotated view)     flip 1140..1161
#     3. Qd1-h5  (White, normal view)       flip 1460..1481
#     3... Ng8-f6 (Black, rotated view)     flip 1760..1781
#     4. Qh5xf7# (White, normal view)       flip 2080..2101
# - Qxf7# triggers the pawn-shaped iris wipe into the Western Queen-takes-Pawn capture cartoon
#   (12 stereo MS ADPCM sound effects), then returns via iris wipe to the board with the
#   "Checkmate! Congratulations, you win!" dialog and its checkmate fanfare.
# - (320,232) clicks the green tick on the checkmate dialog (flip 4260, let go at poll 300),
#   returning to the throne room (freeing the engine allocation with GlobalUnlock/GlobalFree).
# - Closing the window at flip 4310 exits 0 cleanly.
